When a rendering update reports the Event Timing entries of the events
before it, Ladybird reports them before any task after the update runs.
WebKit does the same: Page::updateRendering() runs Document::
enqueueEventTimingEntriesIfNeeded() as its EventTiming step. So does
Gecko: PerformanceMainThread::DispatchPendingEventTimingEntries() runs
from a post-refresh observer right after the refresh driver’s tick,
with no script between. Blink reports them later, once the frame’s
presentation promise resolves, in WindowPerformance::OnPresentation-
PromiseResolved(). But it takes each duration from that frame’s
presentation time, so a task that runs before the report can never
make an entry longer than it was.
